From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hendra Manudinata <manoedinata@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:49:40 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 091/108] misc: modem_v1: build cleanly with GCC and
 CONFIG_WERROR

OpenWrt builds the kernel with GCC and CONFIG_WERROR=y, which turns the
downstream code's warnings into errors. Fix them:

- modem_main.c copied MAX_MIF_SEPA_SIZE (32) bytes out of the 4-byte
  "size" into the IPC logger header, reading 28 bytes of stack; copy
  sizeof(size).
- stop_net_ifaces() tested "!atomic_read() > 0", which parses as
  "(!x) > 0"; netif_stopped is 0 or 1, so write the intended "!x".
- modem_notify_event() takes the modem_state that enum modem_event
  mirrors; make the conversion explicit.
- Mark the two intended fall-throughs.
- "static const char const *" and "static const inline char *" become
  "static const char * const" and "static inline const char *".
- modem_variation.h declares every modem and link constructor, not only
  the configured ones, so the dummies have prototypes too; the files
  that define the real ones include it, mcu_ipc.c includes its own
  public header (the private mcu_ipc.h, which shared its include guard,
  gets its own guard and takes enum mcu_ipc_region from it), the unused NAPI poll (mem_netdev_poll()) is only built with
  CONFIG_LINK_DEVICE_NAPI like the rest of the NAPI code, and the two
  ss310ap exports are
  declared in modem_prj.h.
- The pm_qos stubs in compat.h evaluate their arguments, so the request
  objects are no longer unused.
- pr_buffer() uses a fixed 16-byte (48-character) buffer instead of a
  VLA; every caller passes max_len 16.
